.TH CCODE 1 "August 2026" "ccode v0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ccode \- terminal AI coding assistant (TUI frontend)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ccode
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ccode
is the interactive terminal UI for the
.B ccode
coding agent.
It renders the conversation in an ANSI terminal, streams assistant output
as it arrives, shows tool permission prompts, and manages input history.
All agent work is delegated to the backend executable
.BR ccode-cli (1),
which is spawned automatically (override with
.B \-\-backend
or
.BR CCODE_BACKEND ).
.PP
The TUI is always interactive: no
.B \-i
or prompt flag is required. A bare
.B ccode
starts the UI, and options such as
.B \-\-thinking
or
.B \-\-write
are forwarded to the backend.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-api-base " URL"
OpenAI-compatible API base URL (defaults to
.BR CCODE_API_BASE ).
.TP
.BI \-\-api-key " KEY"
API key (defaults to
.BR CCODE_API_KEY ).
.TP
.BI \-\-model " NAME"
Model name (defaults to
.BR CCODE_MODEL ).
.TP
.B \-\-thinking
Send the
.B "thinking"
field
.RB ( type:
.BR enabled ).
Independent of
.BR \-\-reasoning .
.TP
.B \-\-reasoning
Send the reasoning_effort field (default effort:
.BR medium ).
.TP
.BI \-\-reasoning-effort " LEVEL"
Reasoning effort:
.BR low ", " medium ", " high ", " xhigh
or
.BR max .
Implies reasoning on.
.TP
.BI \-\-thinking-effort " LEVEL"
Alias for
.BR \-\-reasoning-effort .
.TP
.B \-\-write
Enable read and write tools (write_file, edit_file, bash, run_command,
web_fetch, ...) with interactive confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-read-only
Read-only tools (read_file, glob, grep, git_*). This is the default mode.
.TP
.B \-\-default
Fast start preset: interactive UI plus read/write tools plus thinking.
Never enables
.BR \-\-auto-approve .
.TP
.B \-\-auto-approve
Approve every tool request without asking. Equivalent to
.BR CCODE_AUTO_APPROVE=1 .
.TP
.B \-\-allow-http
Allow
.BR http://
API endpoints beyond loopback (also
.BR CCODE_ALLOW_HTTP=1 ).
Plaintext traffic, known risk. Loopback http is always allowed.
.TP
.B \-\-no-markdown
Disable markdown rendering (raw output).
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " PATH"
Path to the
.B ccode-cli
backend executable (defaults to one next to the ccode binary, or
.BR CCODE_BACKEND ).
.TP
.BI \-\-save-session " PATH"
Save the conversation to
.I PATH
after each prompt.
.TP
.BI \-\-resume " PATH"
Load a conversation from
.I PATH
before the run.
.TP
.BI \-\-session-dir " DIR"
Session storage directory (defaults to
.BR CCODE_SESSION_DIR ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.SH TUI KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Submit the input line.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-C
Cancel the in-flight request (press twice to quit).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-D / Ctrl\-Q
Quit the TUI.
.PP
Additional editing keys follow common readline conventions (arrows,
home/end, backspace, etc.).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
See
.BR ccode-cli (1)
for the full list. Relevant to the TUI:
.TP
.B CCODE_BACKEND
Path to the backend executable.
.TP
.B CCODE_WORKSPACE
Workspace directory (defaults to the current directory).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ccode/sessions/
Conversation session files (JSON).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ccode-cli (1),
.PD 0
